next: Issue #357 first milestone is merged into dev via PR #361 (446cf12d); post-merge coverage passes, plan reconciled and merged branch/worktree removed. Global certificates and broad cross-API reporting remain deferred; no further implementation or release is authorized. 0.15.0 shipped; the obsolete `medfit.native_defaults` option is removed on dev (#351), docs refreshed (#352) and the pkgdown Articles menu updated (#353). Fixed: the `gates (rest)` mutants self-test failure on dev (native-defaults control, "the baseline itself is bad") came from #351 renaming the combo "optin" to "unset" while tests/sim/results/native-defaults-oracle-2026-10-24.csv kept 119 "optin" rows; #354 relabeled them (data only) and merged to dev, and both gates shards pass (run 40443220309). Semopy oracle PR #356 merged to dev as 469a2b53; Ubuntu OpenBLAS QC rest (149/149) and reliability (6/6) passed on PR head 296951d (run 40583565985). Session cleanup: merged worktrees removed; release-0-15-0 and feature-d4-typed-covariance retained with their local evidence. Historical evidence and session records archived in ignored _agents_workspace/historical-evidence-2026-10-27.zip and _agents_workspace/worktree-records-2026-10-27.zip (local only). D4 PR #358 is merged into dev (b9af937a); plan and status reconciled, verified evidence archived for merged-branch/worktree cleanup. Preserve release timing.csv and sem-fixed-x-gate-2026-10-26.csv. Later: the OpenMx/semopy syntax page (planning/specs/BRAINSTORM-semopy-oracle-2026-10-24.md). CRAN deferred (#83 closed 2026-10-22; GitHub-only releases continue); no patch release before the next planned one (author, 2026-10-21): #292 and #290 ride with it. #276 closed. Gates runner is OpenBLAS, see memory gates-runner-uses-openblas.
d1_ledger_p1: 2026-10-25 - MERGED to dev, PR #336 (`c052baa`). Plan `planning/PLAN-missingmed-evidence-D1-D4-2026-10-24.md` P1; decisions ADR D-12 and the NOTE-D1 reconciliation table (field `ledger`, class `medfit_error_ledger`). Native fits, branches and `mbco_sem()` keep a versioned outcome ledger; the D-11 error carries `$ledger` and `$best_survivor`. Gates: `sem-fixed-x-gate.R` and `sem-nonlinear-gate.R` (clean and every mutant) pass on the macOS reference BLAS; not run: the OpenBLAS runner (`gates.yaml` dispatch). Next: P2/P3.
d2_certificates_p2: 2026-10-25 - MERGED to dev, PR #338 (`390280e`). Plan `planning/PLAN-missingmed-evidence-D1-D4-2026-10-24.md` P2; reconciliation table in `planning/specs/NOTE-D2-literal-certificates-2026-10-22.md`. A branch with a literal `a == 0` and a nonzero literal equality on the same label is certified empty (proof in the ledger, not fitted); typed `medfit_sem_infeasible` and `medfit_sem_empty_union` refine the D-11 error. Behavior changes are in NEWS. Gates: `test-sem-literal-certificates.R` and both sim scripts clean, every mutant failing, on the macOS reference BLAS; the OpenBLAS runner passed after P4 (see `checkpoint2_missingmed_rerun`).
d3_branch_map_p3: 2026-10-25 - MERGED to dev, PR #339 (`1bd5236`). Plan `planning/PLAN-missingmed-evidence-D1-D4-2026-10-24.md` P3; reconciliation in `planning/specs/NOTE-D3-branch-map-2026-10-22.md`. Zero-product ledger nodes carry `branch_map` (raw count, factor counts, structural IDs, unique count); the 64-raw cap is overflow-safe and checked before the grid is allocated; an over-cap model is refused on the raw count alone (no literal check). Forged maps refuse via `medfit_error_ledger`. No result changes. Gates: full suite 1648 tests, 8059 expectations, 0 failed, 0 errors, 2 skipped (one lme4 warning, same on dev); `sem-fixed-x-gate.R` and `sem-nonlinear-gate.R` clean and every `MUTANT=` failing, on the macOS reference BLAS; the OpenBLAS runner passed after P4 (see `checkpoint2_missingmed_rerun`).
d4_covariance_p4: 2026-10-25 - MERGED to dev, PR #340 (`9599608`). Plan `planning/PLAN-missingmed-evidence-D1-D4-2026-10-24.md` P4; reconciliation in `planning/specs/NOTE-D4-post-fit-evidence-2026-10-22.md`. An accepted fit whose covariance stage fails is a typed ERROR `medfit_sem_covariance_error` (sibling of `medfit_error_no_convergence`, never a fit) carrying `$ledger` (`covariance = "failed"`, `post_fit`) and `$partial`; `mbco_sem()` retains such a null (same statistic, one warning); a union root reports the first failing branch; D-11 no-convergence outranks it. No result changes. Decisions for the author: class sibling, MBCO retains, message unchanged, root attribution. Gates (final, macOS reference BLAS): full suite 1664 tests, 8352 expectations, 0 failed, 0 errors, 2 skipped (one lme4 warning at test-cluster-boot.R:196, same on dev); `test-sem-post-fit.R` 12 tests, 212 expectations; QA added `test-sem-post-fit-qa.R` (24 mutants, 8 of 10 compatibility mutants had survived and are now caught; 3 equivalent or redundant survivors); `sem-fixed-x-gate.R`, `sem-nonlinear-gate.R` and `sem-se-gate.R` clean, every `MUTANT=` failing; the OpenBLAS runner and missingmed's consumer rerun are recorded in `checkpoint2_missingmed_rerun`. QA was the independent D4 review. The worktrees for #335 to #338 are removed; their four local branches were deleted by the author (2026-10-25).
checkpoint2_missingmed_rerun: 2026-10-25 - Checkpoint 2 of the D1-D4 plan, run on dev after P1-P4 merged. missingmed's three consumer files (`test-mbco-encoding.R`, `test-mbco-provider.R`, `test-mbco-sem-acceptance.R`) pass unchanged against dev: 707 expectations, 0 failures, on `c2af811` and `4a84e66`; the closure matrix's 816 is not reproduced (the provider file yields 17), see `planning/specs/RESULT-checkpoint2-missingmed-rerun-2026-10-25.md`. OpenBLAS gates run 40264040502 on dev succeeded (both shards). Target release: a 0.14.x minor. The follow-up fixing MBCO root ledger validation (an ordinary `mbco_sem()` root ledger failed `.sem_valid_outcome()`; new `.sem_valid_mbco_outcome()` runs before return) merged as PR #342 (`524fcb6`); docs sync merged as PR #341 (`e2218c7`).
