zero_product_branch_303: 2026-10-23 - MERGED to dev: PR #303 (`d0d47e7`, squash). A Codex adversarial review of the #300 branch found that `fit_sem()` returned the best surviving zero-product branch with an `incomplete` flag only `mbco_sem()` and `compare_lr()` read, so `coef()`, `vcov()`, `anova()` and `extract_mediation()` could use an uncertified fit. Now `fit_sem()` stops with `medfit_error_no_convergence` (message: failed branches plus the best survivor's discrepancy); `mbco_sem()`/`compare_lr()` already report unresolved; the `incomplete` field is gone. Decision D-11 of `planning/specs/ADR-native-solver-and-engines-2026-10-23.md`; IMPL section 12. Evidence: 138 filtered tests, 0 failed; CI lint, pkgdown, test-coverage, codecov green after one lint indentation fix. Sibling repos: code search only, no `@internals$incomplete` use, suites not run. Not yet in a release: needs the 0.13.0 release PR (NEWS already carries the note).
qc_plan_2026_10_23: 2026-10-23 - MERGED to dev: PR #302 (brainstorm `planning/specs/BRAINSTORM-optimizer-quality-control-2026-10-23.md`, grill Q-1..Q-6, design review R-1..R-6, solver ADR) and PR #304 (`6287f02`, enforcement): `oracle` and `mutants` columns in `tests/sim/gates.csv` with `test-gate-coverage.R` (fails on an empty oracle or mutants list, a mutant name the gate's script lacks, or a driver defect `run-gates.R` does not plant), the structure registry `tests/sim/structures.csv`, `risk-tier.yaml` (seven-item admission checklist for a PR touching `tests/sim/risk-files.txt`; ran green on #304 itself), `qc-weekly.yaml` (renamed `qc-monthly.yaml` and made monthly in #306) with `tests/sim/qc-lib.R`/`qc-metrics.R`/`qc-collect.R` (scheduled gates on dev, history row on the `qc-results` branch, deduplicated issues on a failing gate or a changed R/BLAS/nloptr/lavaan/OpenMx), the ADR YAML decision list with `test-adr-front-matter.R`, and a CLAUDE.md section. Decided: three checks per new model class, seven for high-risk; drift bands after about 8 rows. Not verified: the scheduled workflow has never run on GitHub (scheduled runs use the workflow on `main`, so it first runs after a release; the first manual dispatch creates `qc-results`). Open: make `risk-tier` required after three clean PRs, the generated QC article, R-4 (site snapshot of qc-results), an optional path-filtered gate run on dev PRs.
floor_276: 2026-10-21 - MERGED to dev: #289 (floored oracle), #292 (status -4 accepted when the gate's checks pass, plus a restoration polish before the gate decides; fixes the runner wrong-branch fits on `var-1e6-1e-6`), #290 (floor gate with per-q_tag completeness check after Codex G3). Evidence: 5 of 5 runner gate runs 144/144 after the rebase; status-only change gave 6 of 10. Plan planning/specs/PLAN-floor-comparator-276-2026-10-21.md. Worktrees removed; remote tmp/diag*, tmp/verify-fix-276 and local tmp/* branches are the author's to delete. 2026-10-21 (author): `main` now requires `ubuntu-latest (release)`, `gates (rest)` and `gates (reliability)` (strict); each dev-to-main release PR waits ~25-35 min for the gate shards; undo = PATCH required_status_checks with contexts reduced to the first.
