fixed_x_implementation: 2026-10-13 — MERGED to dev: PR #175 squash `1023520` (CI 10/10; worktree and branch removed). Built on `feature/native-fixed-x` (bundled into 0.9.0, GRILL-native-fixed-x F-G1; supersedes the 0.9.1 note above): V1-V9 and the docs of V10 done, SPEC/PLAN/todo in planning/ and tasks/. 29 harness tests plus the frozen 0.8.0 gate green, full suite 0 failures, strict check 0/0/0, `tests/sim/sem-fixed-x-gate.R` RULE MET (worst fixed-vs-free estimate deviation 2.8e-8; six `MUTANT=` defects exit 1). Decisions made while building: logLik conditional on the fixed block with the means of unfixed variables counted when `meanstructure` is off (lavaan's ms=FALSE count omits them, so parity is checked against its mean-structure fit); `glance()` gains a `fixed_x` column; tests compare structural parameters only. Timing: 30 covariates, 561 to 65 parameters, about 20 times faster (noisy, 20-28). OpenMx subset check done (estimates 1e-4, SEs 1e-3). PR #175 open. R2 done (seed identical to 0.8.0, pinned). Spec and plan approved 2026-10-13. Open: merge call, R1 (tolerance is relative; ubuntu BLAS awaits CI), 0.9.0 release decision.
factor_covariates_0_11_0: 2026-10-16 - MERGED to dev, PR #215 (squash `56f1658`; unreleased, headline candidate for 0.11.0). Factor/character/logical covariates expand to dummies in the native engine (T1-T10: refit map in `fit@internals$factors`, fixed_x, missing data, products, four-way with a factor covariate; a factor treatment or mediator refused by name; a constraint naming a factor points to the label route). Closed out: planted-defect tests (`test-sem-factor-defects.R`), docs/NEWS, three narrow Codex static reviews (no code bug; bootstrap re-expansion per resample documented; product-only mbco is unreachable because rule 9 refuses any product fit), lint and noSuggests CI fixes. Gate `tests/sim/sem-factor-gate.R` stays script-only (like the fixed_x gate). Full suite at merge 6291 pass, 0 fail, 2 skip; strict R CMD check not run. Plan: planning/specs/PLAN-native-factor-covariates-2026-10-14.md. Open: 0.11.0 scope (per planning/PROPOSAL-0.10.1-2026-10-14.md, batch rather than patch); latent means deferred to 1.0.
release_0_11_0: 2026-10-17 - plan planning/PLAN-0.11.0-scope-2026-10-16.md (Option B); its progress table is the record. Merged to dev: T1 #219, T1b #220, T2+T3 #221 (fixes #213; the issue stays open until the release), T4 #222, T5 #225 (exit criteria and three more native gates, 18 gates in `tests/sim/gates.csv`), T5b #226 (reliability regression: the default start is the last `fit_sem()` attempt), T5c #227 (the "experimental" label dropped; D3 reversed by the author), T5d #224 (R-CMD-check on main only; dev is gated locally with `scripts/check-local.sh`), T5e #229 (gates that compare against lavaan fail without it). Evidence 2026-10-17: `run-gates.R --sim`, 18 of 18 gates PASS (105 of 105 checks); full suite 6392 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped. Known limit of the #213 fix: residual variance below 1e-4 of the variable's variance; not covered: nonlinear inequality rows, latent or multi-mediator models, weighted fits, `mbco_sem()` on a model with nonlinear rows. Also merged: #230 (plan), #231 (T6a-c: the Heywood-vs-lavaan test compared nothing, product-test warnings, a `bootstrap-coverage` gate; 19 gates), #232 (T6e). Open: Checkpoint 3, T6g (close #213 and #130 with the release, comment on #214), T6h (cleanup), the release. Out of 0.11.0: four-way bootstrap helper, latent means (1.0), categorical treatment, mediator and endogenous variables (roadmap Next Actions item 6), Ext D module 2, Ext E. Local branches and worktrees to delete by the author: the merged feature, fix, docs and test branches and the worktrees under ~/.git-worktrees/medfit/.
docs_gaps_2026_10_16: 2026-10-16 - CLOSED on dev. PR #216 (`ffdbf2d`: cookbook recipe 21, nine factor-message rows in guide-troubleshooting, glossary 'dummy' and 'reference level') and PR #217 (`30fe8f6`: model page `model-native-factors.qmd` on the landing page, menu and index, tutorial step 10 with the factor built inline, `guide-changes` 0.11.0 rows, `models.qmd` capability row, nine sentence breaks in methods.qmd with the text unchanged). Delta audit and offers: planning/PROPOSAL-docs-gaps-2026-10-16.md. Decided 2026-10-16: no factor column in `mediation_demo`; the docs build the factor inline with `transform(..., cut())`. Reason: 32 test files and a pinned `dim` depend on the dataset, its generator is seed-selected for known answers, and no sibling package uses it. Revisit if a second feature needs a categorical variable (multi-group models) or users ask; if added, append the draw after every existing one and assert the original 8 columns are bit-identical. methods.qmd: the last 10 long paragraphs were split at sentence boundaries (text unchanged modulo whitespace; docaudit scannability flags 0). Open: the live site shows dev docs only after `gh workflow run pkgdown.yaml --ref dev` (last published before #216 and #217). Checks: #216 and #217 ran local CI (lint, spelling, full suite 6322 then 6340 pass, 0 fail, 2 skip); strict R CMD check on dev before #217: Status OK, 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes.
docs_batch_2026_10_13: 2026-10-13 — all merged to dev, strict CI green each: #176 cookbook recipe 18 (`a98bf70`), #177 planning refresh (`6e1a2a0`), #179 stale-docs sweep, refcard row, tutorial Step 9 (`65f76a8`), #180 quickstart/lavaan-comparison lines (`ea979c5`), #178 `mbco_sem()` refits keep `fixed_x`, found by review of #177, test rewritten (`2d991da`). Worktrees and local branches for these are removed; left: the minibook worker's `docs/native-minibook` (5 `native-book-*` chapters, no PR yet) and another session's detached `~/.worktree/medfit/silly-thompson-db0dde`. Not done: `guide-changes.qmd` (0.8.0 only) belongs with the release. 0.9.0 release decision and version bump are the author's; R1 tolerance is relative and ubuntu BLAS passed in CI.
four_way_0_10_0: 2026-10-14 — U1-U9 of planning/specs/PLAN-native-four-way-2026-10-12.md merged to dev, each squash-merged with CI green: #181 `:` token and canonical `m:x` rows (U1, U2, `42337cc`), #187 product-column materialization (U3, `d56e079`), #188 rules 8 and 9 with U5 (a product turns the mean structure on; U5 stacked as #189 on the U4 branch, `500423d`), #190 model-test policy and information refusal (U6, `ed86a1b`), #191 native four-way extraction (U7, `c1ef255`), #192 native oracles and colon-path gates (U8, Checkpoint B met, `1acd43b`; prep #184), #193 docs, NEWS, lavaan-comparison row (U9, `c205430`). Also #183 native minibook (5 chapters, `7dbff7d`). The 0.9.0 release shipped first (#185) so the half-built `:` path (parses before U3 could fit it) never released. Lessons: dev went red between #187 and #188 because #184's native oracle tests and U3 only fail together (U5 supplies the mean structure), so a PR green on its own base is not green on dev; sibling PRs were re-tested after `gh pr update-branch`. Planted-defect tests need `fx_skip_covr()` (CI runs covr); gate scripts evaluated in tests need the package namespace as parent env. Demand check (GRILL H4) answered by the author: go. Open: the 0.10.0 release decision; follow-ups from #183 (methods.qmd Jacobian and step-size wording); the stale TEST-ONLY comment above `.sem_chisq()` in R/sem-anova.R; AIC()/BIC() still rank fits that anova()/mbco_sem() refuse; the docs' error-message tables are not test-covered.
agent_instructions_sync: 2026-10-13 UTC — condensed AGENTS.md committed and pushed to dev as b2c3c4a. Its referenced local archive was verified byte-identical to the original instructions at 3158f85. Documentation-only change; git diff --check passed, package tests/checks not rerun. dev matched origin/dev before this status follow-up; regular push and post-push synchronization requested. Local .codex/guard-session-counts preserved untracked. Package release/CRAN holds and implementation next actions unchanged.
ext_d: 2026-09-25 — multilevel mediation. Lit review (`5aa7653`, planning/specs/REVIEW-multilevel-mediation-2026-09-25.md) → grill D1-D16 (planning/specs/GRILL-multilevel-mediation-ext-d-2026-09-25.md) → module-1 spec APPROVED (planning/specs/SPEC-multilevel-mediation-2-1-1-2026-09-25.md; `474efdf` draft, `2775300` revision 2 after two adverse reviews that found 5 blockers, `46ff70a` approval). Module 1 = 2-1-1 (cluster-level treatment): new class ClusterMediationData from cluster-mean-centered lmer fits, nie() = a*b_B, own/spillover split in decompose(), KR df for path t intervals, cluster bootstrap; 1-1-1 and sigma_ab are module 2. Delivery PR A (extract) → PR B (fit engine) / PR C (cluster bootstrap). Plan APPROVED 2026-10-08 (planning/specs/PLAN-multilevel-mediation-2-1-1-2026-10-08.md, T0–T15, decisions P1–P14). 2026-10-08: PR A #90 merged to dev `60f2fa2`; PR B #92 open (`feature/cluster-fit`, worktree ~/.git-worktrees/medfit/feature-cluster-fit; includes a fix to the Talloen et al. 2016 reference that #90 cited wrongly, verified against Crossref); PR C #91 open and CI green (`feature/cluster-boot`, worktree ~/.git-worktrees/medfit/feature-cluster-boot; still carries the wrong reference text until rebased on #92). Both edit the plan file's decisions table, so expect a conflict at the second merge. Release assignment decided 2026-10-08: Ext D module 1 = 0.6.0, native SEM = 0.7.0. All three PRs (#90, #91, #92) merged to dev 2026-10-08 and the simulation rerun on dev passed (49 gated checks, 0 failed; results CSV refreshed, `86af59a`). Docs follow-ups merged: #93 (ClusterMediationData in the extraction, introduction and bootstrap articles) and #94 (reference card `vignettes/articles/refcard.qmd`, its coverage test, and planning/specs/SPEC-refcard-cookbook-2026-10-08.md, approved; T0-T2 done, cookbook T4-T5 open). Also merged to dev 2026-10-09: #95 (clear error for random-effect terms in fit_mediation(engine = "lmer") formulas), #96 (docs audit fixes: News @-mention links on the live site, README cluster quick start, roadmap and status text), #97 (cookbook, ten recipes, plus its consistency test): SPEC-refcard-cookbook is complete. All Ext D and docs worktrees and local branches are removed. github.com web pages time out from this machine (API works), so urlchecker cannot run locally; CI and a later retry cover it.
cran_0.3.2_accepted: medfit **0.3.2 ACCEPTED ON CRAN, published 2026-07-23** (confirmed live on https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/medfit/index.html). First submission attempt (2026-07-21, commit 9b4d377) was `[CRAN-pretest-archived]` over a Debian NOTE (S7 Rd files missing explicit `@usage`); fixed via 5 S7 Rd `@usage` signatures + `ParallelMediationData` codoc (commit `fc7b39c`, PR #55). Resubmitted 2026-07-23: confirmation-link clicked 16:50, uploaded 16:51, `[CRAN-pretest-publish]` received 16:57 ("package medfit_0.3.2.tar.gz is on its way to CRAN"; flavors `r-devel-linux-x86_64-debian-gcc` + `r-devel-windows-x86_64` both `Result: OK`) — for a routine update (not a `[CRAN-pretest-newbies]` new-package submission), pretest-publish IS the terminal notification; no separate acceptance email follows. GitHub pre-release promoted to full 2026-07-23 (`gh release edit v0.3.2 --prerelease=false --latest`, confirmed `isPrerelease:false`). Unblocks Stage 2 / probmed (Imports medfit ≥0.3.0). Independent now: medrobust CRAN prep (6 TODOs + NEWS/DESCRIPTION drift); RMediation 1.6.1 already CRAN-submitted 2026-07-21 (see its own .STATUS).
aspell_iteration: DESCRIPTION-only aspell NOTE took 2 rounds to fully explain — round 1 fixed "VanderWeele" (PR #51/#53), win-builder recheck then surfaced a DIFFERENT note on "RMediation medrobust probmed" (same DESCRIPTION text, unchanged) instead of clearing to 0 notes; extended `.aspell/defaults.R`'s ignore list to all 4 words (PR #54). Root cause of the note "moving" rather than clearing is unconfirmed (likely win-builder-side aspell dictionary/environment variance across separate check runs, not a code regression — git diff -w confirmed no DESCRIPTION text change between rounds). Either outcome (0 notes or 1 explained note) is CRAN-submission-safe.
version_bump: 0.4.0→0.5.0 (2026-09-24) — minor bump for result-changing fixes #81 (serial te()/pm()) and #82 (confint path rows); GitHub-only release per planning/specs/GRILL-0.5.0-release-2026-09-24.md. Previous: 0.3.1→0.3.2 (2026-07-20) to avoid colliding with an existing public v0.3.1 tag.
ci_flake_fixed: `ubuntu-latest (release, noSuggests)` job failed twice with "no package called 'testthat'" on identical commits (PR #52 + its main merge) — root cause: `dependencies: "hard"` excludes Suggests for extra-packages too, so testthat install was left to chance. Fixed by pinning `any::testthat` explicitly in `.github/workflows/R-CMD-check.yaml` (commit 8e23a0a, via a spawned background session) — confirmed clean on PR #53 and its main merge, no more reruns needed.
lint_gate: ⚠️ 2026-07-16 — lintr 3.4.0 (published 00:10 that day) tightened `indentation_linter` and turned the `lint` job RED on every PR, days before the 0.3.1 CRAN window. CI installs lintr fresh from RSPM each run and sets LINTR_ERROR_ON_LINT=true, so an upstream release can break the gate overnight with no local change: identical R code passed on 3.3.x (#48, 06-22) and failed on 3.4.0 (#49, 07-16). FIXED by PR #50 — reindented 11 function signatures 4→2 spaces (whitespace only; `git diff -w` empty; 806 tests pass). NOT configurable away: no `indentation_linter` setting accommodates 4-space (hanging_indent_style tidy/always/never = 1/2/8 lints), and `styler --strict` produces 2-space too, so lintr 3.4.0 aligned with tidyverse's own formatter rather than regressing. Lesson: verify `lint` green immediately before any CRAN submission — a passing run from weeks ago proves nothing.
cran_0.3.1_check: ✅ 2026-07-20 — strict incoming-CRAN check (--as-cran --run-donttest, DEPENDS_ONLY/SUGGESTS_ONLY, CRAN_INCOMING_REMOTE) = 0/0/0 locally after 3 fixes: Date field bump (37f14f6), `.Rbuildignore` `.remember` leak — also fixed across mediationverse/medrobust/missingmed/rmediation, probmed+medsim already had it (37f14f6 + 4 sibling-repo commits), aspell WORDLIST gaps + 1 hyphenation reword (9980bb6). `urlchecker::url_check()` clean (17/17). Reverse-dep check: RMediation (only CRAN revdep, Suggests-only) 307/307 tests pass against 0.3.1. Win-builder (all 3 flavors: R-release 4.6.1, R-oldrelease 4.5.3, R-devel r90279) all report the SAME 1 NOTE — "Possibly misspelled words in DESCRIPTION: VanderWeele" (cited author surname; local check missed it, no `aspell` binary on this machine — see CLAUDE.md). FIXED via `.aspell/defaults.R` (`description <- list(ignore = c("VanderWeele"))`, PR #51, merged 431c1e5, feature/aspell-ignore-description worktree cleaned up) — not yet re-verified against a live aspell/win-builder round, but even if it recurs it's CRAN-safe to submit with as an explained NOTE. `cran-comments.md` resynced (c84eedb, then updated post-#51). **Submission-ready.**
done: 2026-06-22: gitignored devtools CRAN-SUBMISSION artifact (anchored /CRAN-SUBMISSION) + removed stale v0.2.0 marker — PR #47 merged to dev (10/10 CI green). Stage-1 cascade COMPLETE (2026-06-18); medfit 0.2.1 on CRAN. RMediation 1.5.0 released (GitHub, pre-release strict checks 0/0/0 ✅) + CRAN-submitted 2026-06-20 (pkg_id 345448, awaiting acceptance). mediationverse + medsim: Remotes dropped, medfit ≥0.2.0 pinned.
watcher: Daily remote routine "medfit-cran-watch" (trig_018qiNZMTUP5Az2UGXyv6vRf, 9am America/Denver) checks the CRAN page + Gmail and reports ACCEPTED / ACTION REQUIRED / STILL PENDING. Runs: https://claude.ai/code/routines/trig_018qiNZMTUP5Az2UGXyv6vRf
release_closeout: 2026-07-24 — PR #56 (dev→main, the @usage fix + status docs, closes #55) merged `04b781e`; `v0.3.2` tag force-moved from stale pre-fix commit to `04b781e` (non-force delete+recreate workaround, since branch-guard's `--force` substring match blocked a direct `git push --force` on the tag even though no branch history was touched); GitHub release notes rewritten from "submitted to CRAN" → "accepted, published on CRAN". Follow-up PR #57 backfilled a NEWS.md gap (the 0.3.2 entry predated the @usage fix, so it didn't mention it) — merged `bc2f081`, dev fast-forwarded to match. main/dev fully synced, all CI green (lint/test-coverage/pkgdown/R-CMD-check). **medfit 0.3.2 release fully closed out.**
extensions: Ext A (parallel mediation) COMPLETE — class (#34), lm/glm extractor+confint (#36), lavaan extractor+vignette+pkgdown (#37) ALL MERGED to dev. Structural trio (simple/serial/parallel) now closed across lm/glm + lavaan. Ext B (VanderWeele 4-way interaction) COMPLETE — spec at planning/specs/SPEC-interaction-fourway-2026-06-03.md. PR B1 (InteractionMediationData class, 35 tests, #38) + PR B2a (lm/glm extraction + decomposition/m_star + delta confint, 27 tests, #39) + PR B2b (lavaan extraction + vignette, 22 tests, #40) ALL MERGED to dev. Four-way decomposition (CDE/INTref/INTmed/PIE) now ships across lm/glm + lavaan. Ext C (engine adapter) SPEC'D + GRILLED 2026-08-22 — target swapped CMAverse→regmedint after review found CMAverse isn't on CRAN and simulation-based effects have no correct slot given nie()/nde()'s live-computed contract; no registry/Decomposition-class abstraction added (YAGNI, verified fit_mediation()'s real dispatch is a 2-line switch). Spec: planning/specs/SPEC-engine-adapter-architecture-2026-08-22.md; ledger: planning/specs/GRILL-engine-adapter-architecture-2026-08-22.md. CMAverse deferred to blocked Ext C.1. Toolchain: roxygen2 8.0.0 migration = issue #35 (done).
release_0.7.0: 2026-10-10 — medfit 0.7.0 released. Bump PR #126 squash `5854eae` (tree 35ca643, the tree every gate ran on; checked equal on origin/dev after the merge and again before the release PR). Release PR #127 (dev to main) merged as `e888947` by GitHub auto-merge with the SQUASH method, enabled from the author's account 27 s before the merge; the plan was a merge commit. Both trees are 35ca643, so `main` carries identical files; back-merge `e2e5b32` (no-ff, empty diff) restored main as an ancestor of dev. Tag `v0.7.0` (lightweight) on e888947 after all 9 main checks went green; GitHub release published as Latest 2026-10-11 01:35 UTC; #105 and #106 closed by the merge. Gates (NOT_CRAN=true): suite 3320 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; strict check (--run-donttest, DEPENDS_ONLY, SUGGESTS_ONLY, CRAN_INCOMING and REMOTE) 0/0/0; lint, spelling, urlchecker clean; constrained gate worst relative SE 1.4e-05 vs OpenMx (120 fits, stationarity rule met); parity gate SE 1.6e-04 with 2 of 420 estimate gaps, both latent n = 50 with lavaan within 1e-6 (D22), memory_exp within 1e-6; S17b probmed gate 17 passed, 0 skipped. Dependents, baseline 0.6.0 vs candidate 0.7.0 compared per test with no difference: RMediation 148 tests / 426 expectations, probmed 172 / 530, missingmed 425 / 1636 (lavaan 0.7-3), mediationverse 36 / 112, 0 failures in any arm; clones of dev: rmediation 7c218e6, probmed 5c6d837, missingmed f0cf491, mediationverse 9b1068e. Codex: the adversarial review of the plan (3 findings, all applied to the plan: assertion-level G11, tree-equality G12, the model-advice correction) and a native review of the release diff (no actionable findings). Decisions: planning/specs/GRILL-medfit-0-7-0-release-2026-10-10.md (R1-R11), plan planning/specs/PLAN-medfit-0-7-0-release-2026-10-10.md.
model_arg_advice_fix: 2026-10-10 — PR #125 squash-merged to dev `fd86211`. NEWS and the roxygen `@param model` said to spell out the glm() argument, but `model` is declared before `...`, so `model = FALSE` and the partial `mod = FALSE` both bind to it and the glm engine errors on any non-NULL value (R/fit-glm.R:238-239); glm()'s own `model` cannot be passed through. Advice corrected to drop the argument, no forwarding mechanism in 0.7.0 (ledger R11); a test pins both spellings.
edge_case_fixes: 2026-10-10 — PR #128 MERGED to dev `fa1f0d5` (`fix/lmer-offset-joint-alignment`; `fc40aad`, `53c21a7`, `76dbf35`, `f3d0df4`). Three findings of the post-release Codex adversarial review, each reproduced on 0.7.0 and fixed test-first: (1) engine = "lmer" rebuilt formulas from term labels and silently dropped offset(); it now errors; (2) the joint alignment guard compared row names only, so a mediator model on a reordered frame with reset row names passed and the M1-M2 cross block was wrong (NIE interval about 16% too narrow, parallel mediators with correlated errors; serial chains are unaffected); the guard now compares the values of shared variables; (3) na.exclude pads residuals() with NA, which filled the joint covariance and the effect intervals with NA, and made a Gaussian glm stop extract_mediation() (found beyond the review). Suite 3340 / 0 / 3, lint and spelling clean. No dependent uses engine = "lmer" or na.exclude. Ship as 0.8.0 (correctness exemption, CLAUDE.md). None of the three is a 0.7.0 regression.
website_review: 2026-10-10 — PR #129 MERGED to dev `1a86a5d` (10/10 checks green; fixes all three below, plus a test that runs cookbook recipes 1-8 after the setup chunk alone, with a planted defect, and version-prerequisite notes on the cookbook, refcard and Getting Started). A Codex adversarial review of the site (cookbook, vignettes, refcard, ADHD-friendliness) returned three findings, each reproduced: HC3 is offered as survey-weight inference (cookbook.qmd l.75-77, repeated in Getting Started) though it ignores clusters, strata and replicate weights; the README lists a CRAN install first although 0.3.2 lacks mediation_demo and the native and cluster exports; cookbook recipes 2 and 6-8 reuse `fit_m` and relatives from earlier recipes. Unreleased until 0.8.0.
docs_audit: 2026-10-10 — an audit of the site and the Rd files found the live site healthy (40 sitemap pages served, 0.7.0 news live, no internal-doc leak, `pkgdown::check_pkgdown()` clean) and four content gaps, all docs-only, fixed in PR #131 (squash-merged to dev `6cd95e2` at 20:35 MDT, 10/10 checks green, auto-fix on): G1 Getting Started lacked the cluster and native engines; G2 `?extract_mediation` omitted the `SEMFit` method and named `brms` as supported; G3 the Introduction and Model Extraction articles never mentioned the native engine; G4 `?SEMFit`, `?SEMFit-methods` and `?"medfit-syntax"` had no examples. Not audited: ADHD-friendliness of the long articles (`extraction.qmd` is 931 lines). Unreleased until 0.8.0.
readme_audit: 2026-10-10 — all seven README example blocks were run on 0.7.0 and compared with the printed outputs: six matched, the bootstrap block did not (README showed `NIE = 0.19 [0.08, 0.32] | NDE = 0.16 | PM = 55%`; actual, identical across two runs with seed 42, `NIE = 0.164  [0.0867, 0.256] | NDE = 0.293 | PM = 36 %`). PR #134 (`7914291`, MERGED to dev `b1f307b` 2026-10-10) fixed it, updates "1,900+ tests" to "3,300+" (last full run 3,340 / 0 / 3), and added the `lmer` engine, `SEMFit` extraction and cluster decomposition to the README feature and function lists. The README has no source file, so its outputs are pasted by hand. #136 then rewrote it as the home page (What's new table, 60-second start, Pick your model table, folded long examples, class and function tables). Unreleased until 0.8.0.
model_pages: 2026-10-10 — gap analysis in `planning/specs/GAP-docs-model-pages-2026-10-10.md` (committed on `docs/model-pages`): six gaps (no menu by model, no page per model type, no worked example for the `regmedint` engine, a binary mediator or native serial and parallel, the native one-mediator limit undocumented, no capability matrix, no `articles:` index). Verified by running: `fit_mediation(engine = "native")` takes one mediator (errors "Must have length 1"); native serial and parallel go through `fit_sem()` then `extract_mediation(structure = )`. pkgdown groups Quarto articles only with entries written as `'`articles/<name>`'` in `_pkgdown.yml` (bare, double-quoted and backticked-bare names all fail). Decisions (author took the recommendations): two PRs, the landing page beside the cookbook, the Cookbook menu lists all 11 recipes. Status 2026-10-11, DONE: the docs overhaul is merged to dev in five PRs, each only on an explicit go-ahead. #135 (`b3421d1`) the Models and Cookbook menus, the grouped articles index, the Models landing page with a capability matrix and eight model pages (simple, glm families, interaction, weights, regmedint, serial, parallel, joint); #136 (`a5873f5`) the home page and a four-step Getting Started; #137 (`b55dfe2`) six more pages (cluster 2-1-1, lavaan, and four native: paths and defined parameters, a latent mediator, constraints and MBCO, several mediators and weights); #139 (`52026c9`) a Guides menu and group with What changed since CRAN 0.3.2, Troubleshooting (about 40 messages, each triggered by a test), Which interval should I use? and a Glossary. Tests: `test-model-pages.R` (66), `test-model-pages-messages.R` (10), `test-guide-pages.R` (23), `test-guide-changes.R` (18), `test-guide-troubleshooting.R` (61, cases needing `regmedint` or `lme4` skip when absent: the noSuggests job failed on them until `de45440`). Corrections made on the way: the cluster page first said "no random slopes" (a slope on the within-cluster mediator term is accepted; on the treatment, the cluster mean or the raw mediator it is rejected); a message-quote test must not abort on the first missing Suggests package. Found and fixed separately: `nobs()` overstated rows under missing values (#138). Still open from the proposal (`planning/specs/PROPOSAL-more-articles-2026-10-10.md`, 16 ideas ranked): plotting, reporting, missing data, the native syntax guide, from-other-tools, the `mediation_demo` tour, a model-chooser flowchart; none scheduled. Unreleased until 0.8.0.
stale_content_check: 2026-10-10 — a check of the refcard, cookbook and articles for stale content (no tutorial sources exist in the repo; `docs/tutorials` is an empty ignored local build) found three problems, fixed in PR #133 (squash-merged to dev `17d976d`, 10/10 checks green): the Introduction called `SEMFit` "a seventh class" (an error introduced in #131; 8 classes are exported, so it is the eighth), the refcard gave `joint_effects(x, theta)` where the arguments are `(object, estimates)`, and the Introduction's Package Ecosystem list omitted probmed and medrobust behind a hidden "future packages" comment. Verified still true: the weights example SEs (NIE 0.0640, NDE 0.109), the serial chain share (0.075 of 0.367), the four-way non-Gaussian error, the refcard and cookbook argument names, the cookbook's eleven recipes, and the version strings. Not checked: the Kenward-Roger "1.000 to 1.002 at J = 15" ratios in methods.qmd and the README's printed outputs. The plain `/rforge:r:site` build failed on this machine because the installed medfit was 0.4.0 (the articles run code that needs 0.7.0); medfit 0.7.0 is now installed in `/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.6/site-library` from the `v0.7.0` tag (e888947, not the dev tip), and the plain build passes (`status: ok`, built, no problems). Its 12 advisory leak findings were all false positives (CI strips CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md, and the vignettes hits are the real articles); `.rforge.yaml` (`site.allowlist`, a8a3ac6 on dev, with `^\.rforge\.yaml$` added to `.Rbuildignore`) allowlists them and `lib.sitelint` now reports 0 findings. Unreleased until 0.8.0.
scannability_audit: 2026-10-10 — an audit of article length and structure (measured by a prose-word, heading, chunk and paragraph scan; no reader test) found four gaps, all fixed in PR #132 (squash-merged to dev `8bd8987`, 10/10 checks green): `extraction.qmd` had `Next Steps` before two more sections, no route chooser on its 942 lines, and three 113-124 word paragraphs (now 86/84/73 and bullets); `methods.qmd` cluster 2-1-1 (1,142 words) and native engine (959 words) sections had almost no subheads (H3 count 1, now 14). The two 199-207 word math paragraphs in `methods.qmd` are left alone. A first scan wrongly flagged the "Same data, different CI" callout title as an H2; it is a callout, so nothing needed fixing there. Unreleased until 0.8.0.
site_deploy: 2026-10-11 — the docs overhaul (#134-#139) is live: `gh workflow run pkgdown.yaml --ref dev` (run 38149153110, success) moved `gh-pages` to `1a44a6c`, built from dev `90a223c`. Before it the live site was the 0.7.0 `main` build and `/articles/models.html` returned 404. Verified by `curl` after the run: the home page, Getting Started, Models, `model-cluster`, `model-native`, the four guides and `sitemap.xml` (67 pages) all return 200; the home page has the What's new and Pick your model sections and the Models and Guides menus; no render errors on the cluster page. The site is a dev build ahead of a 0.8.0 package, and the next push to `main` or a published release redeploys over it (procedure in memory `medfit-site-deploy`).
harness_fixes: 2026-10-25 - MERGED to dev: #335 squash `9c896ee` (CI 2 pass, 1 skipped). Codex adversarial review fixes to the agent harness: oracle rule asserts row names and counts, gates verdict FAIL until a dev-reproduced failure's waiver is recorded, orchestrator fails closed (gates, docs, final gates; exact `Verdict: PASS|FAIL` last line; scoped commit and clean tree before push; ask before push and PR; reports by run type; Active plan read from CLAUDE.md), tracked Codex copy `.agents/skills/` (worktrees under `.worktrees/`, role files embedded in spawn prompts), `.worktrees` and `.agents` in `.Rbuildignore`. Not run end to end yet: the first plan task (P1, ADR D-12) is the trial.
worktree: 2026-10-25 — `feature/harness-skill-fixes` (#335, merged) and its worktree `~/.git-worktrees/medfit/harness-skill-fixes` await the author's cleanup. Earlier, 2026-10-24 — the nine 0.14.0 worktrees (#321-#328, #330) are removed, each tip checked against its merged PR head; their local branches await the author's delete; `ci-codecov-push-only` (#331, another session) is left. Earlier, 2026-10-11 — after the 0.8.0 release every merged worktree and local branch is removed (the release-cycle branches, `feature/sem-nonlinear-polish`, `claude/vibrant-goldwasser-aa504b`, the four older feature/fix branches and the four `worktree-agent-*`, each verified against its PR head or ancestry and deleted by the author after the branch guard's confirmation). Local branches left: `dev`, `main`, `gh-pages`; no extra worktrees.
plan_0_8_0: 2026-10-11 — 0.8.0 planned (no code started): BRAINSTORM, grill ledger G1-G13, feasibility study and RMediation handoff under `planning/specs/` (d7b3ca1 to 25d0617, Codex and code-review corrections applied), and `tasks/plan.md` + `tasks/todo.md` (24 tasks, 4 checkpoints, 801ed69; Codex review applied d47269b; approved by the author 2026-10-11). The RMediation-rooted session built the OpenMx oracle fixture (d7d2b10) and, at the user's direction, fixed `mbco()`'s class check and the Rd example in Data-Wise/rmediation#36 (open, checks green); results and four corrections to the handoff are recorded in the HANDOFF note. The `(SEMFit, SEMFit)` route stays blocked until `anova()` for `SEMFit` and the nonlinear constraints land; one new constraint for T10 and T14: refit nulls from a clean start (the refit trap). Pending: the rhub run (T2), the `anova()` and gate-fixture details left in G9 and G6. The rforge false version-drift warning on this file's `version:` line (Data-Wise/rforge#84) is fixed by rforge#85, merged 2026-10-11.
rhub_0_8_0_t2: 2026-10-11 — plan task T2 (ledger G4, nloptr CRAN-flavor evidence): `rhub.yaml` dispatched on dev at 2930cf4 with `ubuntu-gcc12,linux,windows,macos-arm64,macos` (run 38162183152, https://github.com/Data-Wise/medfit/actions/runs/38162183152). All five platform jobs and setup succeeded, so nloptr stays in Imports and no Suggests fallback is needed. Not evidence about the 0.8.0 code, which does not exist yet: the run tests dev as of 2930cf4.
progress_0_8_0: 2026-10-11 — Phase 0 and most of Phase 1 done on dev. Merged: #140 foundations (T1 evidence fixtures, T3 gate driver, T4 and T5 named errors, F1 research; `f239345`), #141 T5b glm row-level args (`2c873ed`, fixes the unreleased #138 regression; must be in before the release PR), #142 T3b gate-driver hardening (`cd2bb4c`), #143 T6 redundant inequality rows (`c52bc84`, drop-only rule, implied_tol 1e-12), #144 T7 NNLS sign gate (`7ecbe69`; its planted-defect test was made covr-robust in `35b28ed`). T2 is recorded above (rhub_0_8_0_t2). T8 merged (#146, `83bab2d`) and the T9 fresh-context review is recorded as ledger G14 (planning/specs/GRILL-medfit-0-8-0-2026-10-11.md): F1, F5 and Q14 closed (F1 and F5 with caveats noted there); F4, open narrowly when the review reported (indefinite-Hessian bound accepted, differing bound statistics, bound misattributed beside a wrong-sign inequality), was closed by T8b (#147, `9405360`): no S1 item is open. Checkpoint A evidence, run 2026-10-11 on dev `d4b68ed` from a clean worktree: full unit suite 3934 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors, 3 skipped; lint 0; strict `devtools::check(cran = TRUE, args = "--run-donttest")` with the DEPENDS_ONLY, SUGGESTS_ONLY and CRAN_INCOMING(_REMOTE) variables: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes; `run-gates.R --fast` 3 of 3 (1397 `sem-` tests); `run-gates.R --sim --only parity,constrained` 12 of 12 (parity 420 rows, 418 within 1e-6, max SE 1.62e-04; constrained 120 rows, max est 4.51e-07, max SE 1.42e-05); `--mutants` every mutation rejected, every control passes. Open before Checkpoint A closes: human review; T12 one parameter-naming convention (label, else unspaced `lhs op rhs`, lavaan's; loadings `eta=~m2`) and `weights`/`object` argument names with `lifecycle` deprecations merged ahead of that review (#150, `054c702`); T13 nonlinear equality constraints in review (#151); T10 `anova()` and T11 `tidy()`/`glance()`/`confint()` for `SEMFit` merged ahead of that review (T11 #149: lavaan agreement about 1e-9, `@converged` is always TRUE for a returned fit so `glance()` has no such column; 4049 tests pass, strict check 0/0/0); T10 `anova()` for `SEMFit` merged ahead of that review (#148, `fc80a82`: parameter-table inclusion for nesting, boundary guard at the restricted fit, reproduces the `mbco_sem()` known answers; strict check 0/0/0, 3992 tests pass; the plan's "seed the refit from the full fit" planted defect does not fail in medfit, see the PR); then Phase 2 (`anova()`). Per-task detail in `tasks/todo.md`.
progress_0_8_0_phase3: 2026-10-11 — Phase 3 (T13-T19) merged to dev: #151 nonlinear equalities, #152 zero-product branch split, #153 product inequalities and best-of-n, #154 sums of products (best-effort), #155 `mbco_sem(paths = )`, #156 min-of-k size gate (size at most 0.055 at alpha 0.05 with one zero path, under 0.005 with two or three; power 0.838 against a 0.75 floor; k >= 3 ships), #157 nonlinear parity gate (240 runs, four planted defects each exit 1; found native estimates 3.3e-5 from both oracles, closed by the Newton polish #160: 5.5e-11 from the reparameterized optimum, OpenMx compared at 1e-4). Checkpoint C evidence on dev: strict `devtools::check` 0/0/0 after #158 (undeclared rlang in tests; withr now in Suggests); probmed and RMediation suites against dev medfit in a scratch library: no failures; `run-gates.R --fast` 3 of 3 (1681 `sem-` tests, lint 0); the parity and constrained gate scripts had compared nothing since T12 renamed the parameters (constrained printed PASS on -Inf) and are fixed in #159 (parity 418 of 420 within 1e-6, constrained max SE 1.4e-5). Open: Checkpoint C human review, Phase 4 docs (T20-T22), Phase 5 release (T23-T24).
progress_0_8_0_phase4: 2026-10-11 — Phase 4 (T20-T22) merged to dev: #161 `lavaan-comparison.qmd` (18-row feature table, each status computed from a live lavaan probe by `test-lavaan-comparison.R`; planted edit fails), #162 cookbook recipe 12 and the audit gaps (Newton polish in methods.qmd, the 0.7.0 NEWS claim that `fit_mediation(engine = "native")` handles serial and parallel mediators corrected: it takes one mediator; CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md updated), #163 glm joint-significance recipe (cookbook recipe 13, `joint_test()` with LRT for binomial and Poisson and F for estimated-dispersion families). Cookbook has 13 recipes. Open: Checkpoint D (strict check and site build on dev after #163, human review), T23 release grill, T24 release PR.
release_0.8.0: 2026-10-11 — medfit 0.8.0 released, GitHub-only (grill R1-R3: GRILL-0.8.0-release-2026-10-11.md). Bump PR #164 squash `0958d3f`; release PR #165 (dev to main) merged as a MERGE commit `37171ec` (parents e888947 and 0958d3f, tree equal to dev); all 17 PR checks and the four main workflows (R-CMD-check, lint, pkgdown, test-coverage) green before tagging; lightweight tag `v0.8.0` on 37171ec; GitHub release published as Latest 2026-10-12 03:42 UTC with the NEWS 0.8.0 section. Gates on the release tree: suite 4231 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; strict check 0/0/0; lint 0; URLs 47 of 47; spelling 0; parity 418 of 420 within 1e-6; constrained max SE 1.4e-5; nonlinear gate 240 runs RULE MET; min-of-k size gate at most 0.055; dependents on dev: probmed and RMediation no failures, mediationverse 36 passed, missingmed not run (needs lavaan >= 0.7-3). r-universe pickup complete: /api/packages verified 2026-10-12, Version 0.8.0, RemoteSha 37171ecb8234ef224bce7e18bbc21a412b79bfef, _status success. The back-merge is done (`34008df`, empty diff, main is an ancestor of dev). Docs PR #167 (native step-by-step tutorial; constraints page and introduction updated for nonlinear constraints, `anova()` and `paths =`) merged to dev `4432717`; the site was deployed from dev 2026-10-12 (`gh workflow run pkgdown.yaml --ref dev`, run 38205230382 on 568f187; the tutorial, quickstart and guide pages return 200). T24 complete; E1 version-matrix row merged as Data-Wise/mediation-planning#14, 7b33893f1869b65b5ddf5d0168223f0825d6a28b (2026-10-13 UTC), after review found no actionable issues.
example_data: 2026-09-23 — bundled `mediation_demo` dataset (spec planning/specs/SPEC-bundled-example-data-2026-09-23.md, decisions D1–D10 in planning/specs/GRILL-bundled-example-data-2026-09-23.md). Merged to dev: #62 (D8 guard — multi-mediator extraction now errors on product terms, `aa3362c`), #63 (dataset + data-raw script + known-answer tests + Getting Started article, `44a855c`), #64 (serial docs: keep every mediator in the outcome model, `73280c7`), #67 (PR 2 — roxygen examples + Introduction + Model Extraction articles moved to mediation_demo, `bca59bc`), #65 (Bootstrap article: every chunk runs against the current API on mediation_demo, `af3fa3f`). COMPLETE. Unreleased since 0.4.0; `claude-code-review.yml` workflow removed (`c870d27`). D8(b): spec APPROVED 2026-09-23 (planning/specs/SPEC-joint-mediator-interactions-2026-09-23.md; ledger GRILL-joint-mediator-interactions-2026-09-23.md G1–G9: grill, two adverse reviews via OpenCode, consistency pass, verification harness + outcomes table). Plan drafted: planning/specs/PLAN-joint-mediator-interactions-2026-09-23.md (T0–T10; PR A = T0–T7 core, PR B = T8–T10 methods/docs), APPROVED 2026-09-23. PR A #76 squash-merged to dev `fff0ab7` (2026-09-24): `JointMediationData` class, outcome X:M routing + guards (R/extract-joint.R), reduced-form propagation, stacked-OLS vcov, analytic gradients, effect generics, bootstrap acceptance; oracles vs counterfactual truth + g-computation, planted defects caught, SEs within 3% of B=5000 bootstrap; 1404 expectations, strict 0/0/1, CI 10/10 after one fix (always-on raw-b1 defect check sat at 3.01 SE with mvrnorm MC SEs that vary by LAPACK -> delta SE, n=10000). T0 settled: r-lib check-r-package sets NOT_CRAN=true, so skip_on_cran() oracles run on CI. PR B #77 squash-merged to dev `b40444e` (2026-09-24): print/summary/coef/vcov/nobs/confint/tidy/glance, new export joint_effects() (parametric bootstrap statistic), ?JointMediationData details (estimand, G1, whole-vector assumptions, covariate limitation, precomputed-column warning), Model Extraction section on outcome_int, NEWS. Review fix: joint_effects() errors on missing source rows (was silent zero); tidy()/summary() give NA SEs for hand-built objects. 1441 expectations, strict 0/0/1, CI 10/10. D8(b) COMPLETE. Worktrees feature-joint-core and feature-joint-methods removed 2026-09-24 (local and remote branches deleted). Dead stubs removed in #72.
bootstrap_tidy: 2026-09-23 — PR #66 squash-merged to dev `929f2c5`: parametric/plugin `bootstrap_mediation()` now accept Serial/Parallel/InteractionMediationData (shared `.assert_param_mediation_data()` guard; all four classes carry name-aligned `@estimates`/`@vcov` incl. path aliases), and `BootstrapResult` gains `coef()`/`confint()` (stored interval by default, percentile recompute for another `level`, NA+warning for plugin). A second session added `unname()` in `coef()` (named statistics produced `estimate.a`) and updated the Bootstrap article (#65 had merged first). PR #68 squash-merged `f1ad7b2`: `tidy()`/`glance()` for Parallel + Interaction (path SEs from vcov diagonal; effect/component-row SEs NA like MediationData). Effect SEs in `tidy()`: done in PR #70 (see tidy_effect_se).
tidy_effect_se: 2026-09-23 — PR #70 squash-merged to dev `894bf70` (grill planning/specs/GRILL-tidy-effect-se-2026-09-23.md D1–D7, spec + plan SPEC-/PLAN-tidy-effect-se-2026-09-23.md). One delta-method helper `.effect_se()` (R/effect-se.R) over the @vcov alias rows feeds both `confint(parm = "effects")` and `tidy()` for all four classes; new `confint(<SerialMediationData>)`; `?tidy.S7_object` page. Bug fixes: Simple TE SE dropped Cov(ab, c') (0.1273 -> 0.1194 on mediation_demo); `confint()`/`tidy()` on lavaan-extracted MediationData (located paths by lm-style names). Verified vs lavaan := SEs (1e-6) and parametric bootstrap (3%), planted-error control caught all classes; 1173 expectations, strict check 0/0/1 (Date). Found: custom lavaan path labels zeroed the extractor's alias rows — fixed in PR #69 (`e175453`, shared parTable-based `.lavaan_alias_source_idx()` for all four lavaan extractors, interaction included); merged dev tested at 1191 expectations. Follow-up done: PR #71 (`b2a3ad3`) — lavaan oracle tests extract from the labeled fit (unlabeled-fit workaround dropped; 3-mediator model covers user labels d1/d2 colliding with alias names). PR #72 (`ebd9450`) removed the dead `fit_mediation()`/`bootstrap_mediation()` stubs from R/aab-generics.R (their roxygen had been merged into the real help pages: duplicate usage/value/details, \dontrun examples on nonexistent objects); regmedint + m_star notes moved to R/fit-glm.R. PR #73 (`3954b3c`, from a separate session, #69 follow-up): `.expand_vcov_with_aliases()` errors when a user lavaan label reuses an alias name on a different path (estimate was right, @vcov row was the labeled parameter's); simple lavaan extractor takes alias source rows from a_row/b_row/cp_row, fixing a #69 regression where c_prime followed the treatment argument in the label branch. 1200 expectations, CI 9/9. Remote branch already deleted. PR #74 (`c09d7c8`): extraction detects function-wrapped products like `I(X * M)` (R records them as ordinary covariates, so they bypassed the D8(a) guard and the single-mediator X:M check, returning main effects silently); multi-mediator errors on any wrapped term combining treatment/mediator with another variable, single-mediator errors on wrapped X-by-M and asks for `X * M`. Found by the D8(b) adverse review. 1205 expectations, CI 9/9. PR #75 (`1bae231`): three silent failures found verifying the second D8(b) review (GRILL G8) — `se_type = "sandwich"`/`vcov_fun` now reach the four-way, serial and parallel workers (previously hardcoded `stats::vcov`); four-way requires the identity link (gaussian(link = "log") was accepted); `extract_mediation()` errors on a supplied-but-unused `m_star` (lm/glm + lavaan; call-site keyed). Review fix: `fit_mediation()` forwards `m_star` only when supplied (factor treatments made formula vs coefficient detection disagree). 1224 expectations, strict 0/0/1, CI 9/9.
docs_methods_math: 2026-09-24 — PR #79 squash-merged to dev `9aef925`. New "Methods and Formulas" article (vignettes/articles/methods.qmd, navbar): estimands for all five classes, covariance per engine (lm/glm block-diagonal exact for simple/serial/four-way, omits Cov(a_j, a_j') for parallel; Joint stacked OLS; lavaan joint), delta-method gradients, percentile bootstrap, engines, assumptions. Audit gap report planning/GAP-docs-vignettes-2026-09-24.md (fixed vs open). Rd: all effect pages cover every class; decompose formulas/refs/example; INTref + Joint NDE formulas; extract_mediation lm/glm args; glance/coef/vcov/confint/nobs on ?tidy.S7_object; serial te()/pm() documented as chain-only. Articles/README: confint(parm=) (was type=, silently path CIs), live tidy output with effect SEs. 1439 expectations (+1 confint parm-error test for codecov/patch), strict 0/0/1, CI 9/9. README link to articles/methods.html live since the 0.5.0 deploy. Follow-ups since done on dev: weights/sandwich + non-simple tidy examples (`1f32a25`, `2823952`), articles eval:true (`b888ffe`). Spun off: serial te()/pm() behavior decision; four-way factor-covariate NDE bug.
interaction_factor_covariates: 2026-09-24 — PR #78 squash-merged to dev `4156a38` (from a spun-off session). Four-way E[M | X = 0] now uses the mediator model's design-column means (factor dummies, transformed terms, estimation sample only; case-weighted via model.weights() when weights are supplied), stored on @data so the delta-method gradients reuse them. Was: numeric data columns only, factor dummies silently skipped (NDE off). Independent E2E: NDE = hand to 1e-16, delta SEs within 3% of 400-rep nonparametric bootstrap, weighted NDE = hand. 1476 expectations, CI 9/9.
serial_total_effect: 2026-09-24 — PR #81 squash-merged to dev `3058b90` (from a spun-off session; spec planning/specs/SPEC-serial-total-effect-2026-09-24.md, option (b)). BEHAVIOR CHANGE vs 0.4.0: te()/pm() for SerialMediationData sum every X -> Y path via the recursive path matrix ((I - B)^{-1}), not chain + c'. nie() stays chain-only by default; new nie(type = "total"). Serial lm/glm + lavaan extractors record skip paths as a2..ak, b1..b{k-1}, d{i}_{j}. Hand-built objects missing a present skip-path coefficient -> NA + one warning. coef(type = "effects") appends indirect_total last (positions 1-3 unchanged); tidy/glance gain nie_total. Independent E2E: te = lm(Y ~ X + C) coefficient exactly; lavaan te est/SE = lavaan := to 6 dp. probmed/RMediation do not call serial te()/pm(). 1509 expectations, CI 9/9.
joint_covariate_means_user_data: 2026-09-24 — PR #80 squash-merged to dev `5f911d2` (from a spun-off session). JointMediationData effect SEs with caller-supplied `data =` and factor/poly() covariates: were NA in tidy()/summary() and an error in confint(parm = "effects") (gradients rebuilt covariate means from raw data, which has no terms attribute). Extractor now stores the point estimate's c_bar on @data (`medfit_covariate_means`, same convention as #78); fallbacks kept for hand-built objects. Independent E2E: SEs data=d == data=NULL, delta SEs within 1-4% of 300-rep bootstrap, subset= and no-covariate fits unchanged. 1528 expectations, CI 9/9.
confint_alias_paths: 2026-09-24 — PR #82 squash-merged to dev `c06c898` (from a spun-off session). BEHAVIOR CHANGE: confint(parm = "paths") finds path rows by alias (a, b, c_prime, d1, a1, theta3, ...) then lm-style names, and errors naming missing rows instead of guessing by position. Was: MediationData took the first 3 vcov rows when m_/y_ names were absent — wrong SEs for every lavaan-extracted object (mediation_demo: SE(b) 0.04823 vs lavaan 0.05317, SE(c') 0.0975 vs 0.10909); other classes gave NA bounds. Independent E2E: lavaan path SEs = parameterEstimates exactly; lm = summary(); regmedint runs. Also enabled: articles evaluate at site build (`b888ffe`), pkgdown CI on PRs to dev (first run on #82 passed). CI 10/10.
plan_fixes_lavaan_names: 2026-10-09 — #108 (`dbe5af5`): lavaan-derived simple MediationData gains `m_<X>`/`y_<M>`/`y_<X>` alias rows, so probmed's parametric bootstrap works on the lavaan route (closes #106 at the next main merge; NEWS behavior-change entry in a new development-version section; observed continuous variables only). #107 (`f91d6cf`): `lifecycle` in Imports with badge figures. #109 (`8850f5a`): reviews applied to the native SEM plan, fix spec/plan SPEC-/PLAN-sem-plan-fixes-2026-10-09.md. Owed: comment on #105 with the S17b plan (T15); local branch cleanup is the user's (branch-guard blocks `git branch -D`).
native_sem_plan: 2026-10-09 — PR #104 squash-merged to dev `352ecfc`: planning/specs/PLAN-native-sem-implementation-2026-10-09.md (11 PRs + release, tasks S0-S25, no hour estimates) and its grill ledger GRILL-native-sem-implementation-2026-10-09.md (D1-D8). Decisions: nonlinear constraints in their own PR 11 after checkpoint B (release does not wait); nloptr stays in Imports; MBCO gate asserts both value sets; export fit_sem() + experimental SEMFit; N6 and N7 both in 0.7.0 behind checkpoint B; warn-only multiplier-sign check in 0.7.0, NNLS gate in PR 11. Plan written by an Opus subagent, grilled, then a code review of the two docs found 10 stale/cross-PR issues, all fixed before merge. No code exists yet.
native_sem_pr1: 2026-10-09 — PR #110 squash-merged to dev `6aea7e0` (S0, S3-S6, checkpoint A). Native ML core `R/sem-ml.R`, SE `R/sem-se.R`, driver and acceptance gate `R/sem-optim.R`; nloptr in Imports, OpenMx in Suggests. Checkpoint A (ledger D19): SE tolerance 1e-3, Newton decrement 1e-3, near-singular threshold 1e-4 (author's choice over 1e-3), SLSQP default, preconditioner on (OD3 closed). S2 canary green on all five R-hub platforms; `ubuntu-gcc12` was red on two earlier heads (unexplained, see plan S2). S0(f): NOT_CRAN suite SKIP 12, none in test-sem-*. Local branches feature/sem-core and feature/sem-parser have worktrees under ~/.git-worktrees/medfit.
native_sem_pr2: 2026-10-09 — PR #111 squash-merged to dev `eb77391` (S7-S9): `R/sem-expr.R` locked evaluator and linearity classifier, `R/sem-parse.R` parser and bound folding. 14 core models match lavParseModelString on lavaan 0.7-3; lavaan folds `a < 2*3` but not the mirrored `3 < a` (we fold both), keeps the first of two bounds (we keep the tighter). Review fixes: dangling lhs comma rejected, constant constraint sides guarded at build time. Local branches feature/sem-core, feature/sem-parser and feature/sem-extract-seam (with worktrees) remain.
native_sem_pr3: 2026-10-09 — PR #112 squash-merged to dev `6a3f0fd` (S10, no behavior change): every lavaan read in R/extract-lavaan.R goes through an accessor list (`R/extract-sem.R`, nine fields; 33 calls moved, the plan counted 31 and missed two `lavNames()`). Suite 2623 before, 2649 after. Identity test against a frozen copy of the old extractor (`tests/testthat/helper-frozen-extract-lavaan.R`, linted out in `.lintr`; delete when the seam is retired). CI lint does not source helper files or attach testthat: qualify `testthat::` in file-level test helpers and look up helper-defined functions by name.
native_sem_pr4: 2026-10-09 — PR #113 squash-merged to dev `72c6842` (S11-S12): `R/sem-model.R` (`.sem_complete()` matches lavaanify's row set on 12 spec models and a 1,500-model fuzz, Q3 free exogenous covariances; `.sem_to_partable()`, `.sem_to_ram()`, `.sem_check_scale()`, `.sem_df()`) and `R/sem-fit.R` (`.sem_fit_syntax()`, one listwise deletion). Suite 2649 before, **2821** after (the commit body says 2823, a figure written before measuring). Measured tolerances differ from the plan: Q3 identity 0 to 7e-7 (lavaan's optimizer tolerance, not 1e-8); syntax route vs PR 1 builders pinned at 1e-6 because the noSuggests Linux job saw about 1e-9 (parameter order changes SLSQP iterates). `start(.5)*` on a marker loading: lavaan fixes it at 0.5, ours fixes it at 1 and keeps 0.5 as a start. Constraints (`==`, `<`, `>`, `:=`) error until PR 5.
native_sem_pr5: 2026-10-09 — PR #114 squash-merged to dev `0ff25e2` (S13-S15): `R/sem-constraints.R` (linear rows for `==`, `<`, `>`, `:=` substituted first; projected acceptance gate with warn-only multiplier sign check; shared `.sem_active_set()`), `.sem_vcov()` projects on the active set (V = Z (Z'IZ)^-1 Z'), `.sem_defined()` gives `:=` values and delta-method SEs, `.sem_fit_syntax()` accepts constraints. Suite **2975** passed / 0 failed / 2 skipped. `a == b` covariance equals the collapsed shared-label fit to 5.5e-10; lavaan SEs to 8.6e-9; OpenMx constrained cells worst relative SE gap 1.5e-5 (frozen 1e-3); stationarity rule met (largest converged decrement 3.6e-8, smallest stall 0.014, threshold 1e-3 stands). Not done: `04b` problems not rerun for the stationarity table; bounds warn-only in the projected gate but reject in the plain gate. CI lesson: R-devel `RNGkind()` returns four elements, compare `[1:3]`; sim scripts that call helper functions need an `object_usage_linter` exclusion in `.lintr`.
native_sem_pr6: 2026-10-09 — PR #115 squash-merged to dev `9f56e05` (S16-S18): `fit_sem()`, the `SEMFit` class, `fit_mediation(engine = "native", model = )` (new named argument `model`; `mod = FALSE` now binds to it, in NEWS), `extract_mediation()` for `SEMFit` through the shared lavaan workers (`source_package = "medfit"`), `print`/`summary`/`coef`/`vcov`/`nobs`/`logLik`, probmed gate, `?"medfit-syntax"`, NEWS, methods article, refcard, pkgdown. Suite **3089** passed / 0 failed / 2 skipped. Native vs lavaan extraction to about 1e-9, `logLik` to 1e-8, probmed plugin equal to the lavaan route. **Four-way route unsupported on native fits** (the worker reads the mediator intercept; native has no intercepts): native-specific error, `decomposition = "two_way"` works. Not done: equal-label comparison with lavaan, standardized estimates, weights/sandwich (S21). CI lesson again: file-level test helpers must use `testthat::` and `match.fun()` for helper-defined functions.
native_sem_pr7: 2026-10-09 — PR #116 squash-merged to dev `a010216` (S19-S20): `test-sem-parity.R` (34 expectations), `tests/sim/sem-parity-gate.R`, `memory_exp` fixture (RMediation, GPL >= 3, ledger D23), `sem_openmx()` now converges the oracle at 1e-12. 420 runs across 7 cells: worst SE difference 1.6e-4 (rule 1e-3), estimates within 1e-6 in 418 (worst 1.6e-6, latent n = 50 seeds 4 and 16, OpenMx the loose engine; D22 keeps 1e-6 and records them). MBCO known answers reproduced (221.045546, 0.083100 absolute within 1e-6; as-written example 0.060332). Checkpoint B answered go (D24): PR 8 then PR 9 (D25) for 0.7.0. Not done: the `04b` problems for the constrained stationarity table. Suite 3123 passed / 0 failed / 2 skipped.
native_sem_pr8: 2026-10-09 — PR #117 squash-merged to dev `3668a9c` (S21): `fit_sem(sampling_weights = , se_type = )`, `R/sem-sandwich.R` (casewise scores, weight validation), `.sem_sample(weights = )`, `.sem_vcov(se_type = )`, `fit_mediation(engine = "native", weights = , se_type = "sandwich")`; PR 6 errors for those arguments removed. HC check done first: the native sandwich is HC0 (equals per-equation `vcovHC(type = "HC0")` to 2e-9 and lavaan's `sampling.weights` SEs to 5e-10); the glm route's default HC3 is 1.3-3.7% wider at n = 400, documented in NEWS and the help pages. Weighted estimates equal the glm route to 9e-9. `logLik()` errors for a weighted fit. Suite 3157 passed / 0 failed / 2 skipped. CI lesson: a weight-scale invariance test compared two separate fits at 1e-8 and failed on all Linux and macOS jobs (SLSQP stops at iterates that differ in the last digits); compare at 1e-6 across fits and at 1e-10 at a fixed estimate. Not checked: probmed's nonparametric bootstrap on a weighted native fit would drop the weights.
native_sem_pr9: 2026-10-10 — PR #118 squash-merged to dev `9fb6f95` (S22): `mbco_sem(fit, a, b)` in `R/sem-mbco.R`, the minimum of two linear refits (`a == 0`, `b == 0`), statistic `n_obs * (F_con - F_full)`, df 1, returned as an `htest` (class `c("mbco_sem", "htest")`, so no `registerS3method()` in zzz.R); refuses weighted fits and refits that do not converge. `test-sem-mbco.R`: OpenMx known answers 221.045546, 0.083100 (the minimum) and 0.060332 (Rd example as written) to 1e-6; latent-mediator case equals lavaan constrained fits (CI ran it on 0.7-3; also run locally on 0.7-3 from a scratch library). Planted defect `min` to `max` failed 5 expectations. Full suite 3181 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI. Name `mbco_sem` is the plan's placeholder [A].
native_sem_pr10: 2026-10-10 — PR #119 squash-merged to dev `1ef2403` (S23, docs only): cookbook recipe 11 "A latent mediator, native engine" (simulated three-indicator mediator, `fit_mediation(engine = "native")`, `mbco_sem()`), `test-cookbook-consistency.R` pins eleven recipes, README native-syntax features line and quick start, `"native"` row in the Engines table and the MBCO file-list entries in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md (AGENTS.md brought level with CLAUDE.md), two spelling hits from #118 fixed. Full suite 3181 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; cookbook and methods rendered clean against a scratch install; 10/10 CI.
nonlinear_polish: 2026-10-11 — PR #160 squash-merged to dev `1cc7f02` (10/10 CI green): `.sem_polish()` (`R/sem-constraints.R`) and `.sem_polish_accept()` run after an accepted solve with an active nonlinear row, Newton steps on the KKT system with the Lagrangian Hessian; the acceptance gate is unchanged and re-run, and the polished point replaces the accepted one only if accepted again and the discrepancy did not rise by more than 1e-8. SLSQP had stopped up to 4e-5 short along a flat constraint tangent; native estimates now sit within 5.5e-11 of a reparameterized fit (240 runs). Gate `tests/sim/sem-nonlinear-gate.R` (#157): `est_tol` 1e-5 against the reparameterized fit, separate `omx_tol` 1e-4 against OpenMx (OpenMx is itself up to 4.1e-5 off in 4 inequality runs; an exclusion rule was rejected by an adversarial review because it capped nothing); RULE MET, mutants linear, larger, stale, noproj and the new estoff all exit 1. Unit tests `tests/testthat/test-sem-polish.R` (planted defects: polish off, wrong-direction step, off-constraint point). Full suite 950 tests, 0 failed, lint 0. Fallback scan, seeds 1-50, n = 100, 5 starts each (250 accepted attempts per cell): eq and sum polished 250 of 250 in both structures; ineq simple 242 of 250 (8 rejected by the gate or the discrepancy guard), ineq serial 235 of 250 (15 returned NULL, not diagnosed; probably the inactive inequality branch). Unreleased, ships with 0.8.0.
sem_mixed_jacobian_fix: 2026-10-10 — PR #120 squash-merged to dev `4be8340`: `.sem_nlopt_constraints()` assigned the equality and inequality Jacobians to one name `jac`, the closures share one environment, so a model with `a == 0` beside `b + cp < 1` enforced the inequality row as the equality (fit errored "`a == 0` violated by 4.63e-01"; two equalities plus one inequality errored in nloptr on the Jacobian size). Fix: `jac_eq` and `jac_ineq`. Found by the Codex adversarial review of `main...dev`, reproduced before the fix. Tests (callbacks over four shapes, lavaan oracles at 1e-5 with `rel.tol = 1e-12` because lavaan's default stop sits 3e-6 off its own solution, `fit_sem()`, `mbco_sem()` on a model with an inequality); reverting the fix fails three test blocks. Full suite 3208 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI. Introduced in PR 5 (#114), dev only, so no NEWS entry.
cluster_boot_advisory_fix: 2026-10-10 — PR #121 squash-merged to dev `7d3ac67`: `.bootstrap_nonparametric_cluster()` flagged every warning as a failed refit, but a `fit_mediation(engine = "lmer")` refit always raises the few-cluster advisory below 25 clusters (model SEs) or below 10 (any SE), so every replicate was dropped and the bootstrap errored "Too many bootstrap samples failed" (20 clusters with model SEs, 8 with kr; 40 clusters and kr at 20 worked). Fix: the advisory has condition class `medfit_few_clusters` (R/extract-lmer.R) and the handler (R/bootstrap.R) muffles it uncounted; every other warning still flags. In released 0.6.0 code, NEWS "Bug fixes" entry says `se_type = "kr"` with 10 or more clusters avoids it. Tests: classed warning, replicates kept, other warnings still fail a refit, real 20-cluster `fit_mediation()` bootstrap; reverting fails all four. 3220 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI.
sem_redundant_equalities_fix: 2026-10-10 — PR #122 squash-merged to dev `8dd9b63`: linearly dependent equality rows (a duplicate, `a == b` with `b == a`, a transitive triple, `a == 0 ; b == 0 ; a + b == 0`) gave SLSQP a rank-deficient Jacobian and it stopped with nloptr status -4, so a consistent model failed to fit. `.sem_independent_rows()` (R/sem-constraints.R, pivoted QR, tolerance 1e-8) hands the solver an independent subset in the original order; the gate and covariance keep every row, so `a == 1 ; a == 2` still errors naming a violated constraint. Oracle is the equivalent independent set fitted by the native engine, not lavaan: lavaan 0.7-2 does not converge on several of these shapes and 0.7-3 warns on four of five. 3251 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI.
sem_equality_df_fix: 2026-10-10 — PR #123 squash-merged to dev `6ef3242`: model df, the negative-df guard, `logLik()` df and `print` counted every element of `theta`, so explicit `a == b` gave df 0, logLik df 9 and AIC 2 above its shared-label twin (df 1, logLik df 8), and a model identified only by an equality (free `M ~~ Y` plus `cov == 0`) was rejected as over-parameterized. Fix: the rank of the equality rows (a dependent row removes none) is computed in `.sem_fit_syntax()` before the df check (constraint rows are now built earlier, so a constraint error can precede the over-parameterization error), stored as `internals$eq_rank`, and used by `.sem_df()`, `.sem_n_free()` and `logLik()`. New `test-sem-constraint-df.R` (49 expectations: twin models, lavaan df, planted defect with `.sem_eq_rank` mocked to 0); reverting fails 6 of 7 blocks. 3300 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI. The native `logLik()` counts the three sample means as parameters and lavaan's default does not, so compare twin models, not raw lavaan AIC.
mbco_guards: 2026-10-10 — PR #124 squash-merged to dev `a7d3100`: `mbco_sem()` (R/sem-mbco.R) now refuses labels that are not labeled free `~` regression paths (auto-names, variances, loadings), refuses a full fit that did not converge, has its refits inherit the fit's `n_starts` and `control` (stored in `internals`, R/sem-fit.R and R/fit-sem.R), warns when a bound or an inequality on the tested path is active at its null refit (the null is then on the boundary, a chi-square mixture, p-value not valid; the parser folds `a > 0` into a box bound, so the check reads `active_bounds` as well as the inequality rows, and is scoped to the parameter tested in each refit), and errors clearly when the constraints rule the null out (`a > 0.3`). Corrected finding: `a < 0.2` is statistically fine (the null `a = 0` is interior), so it stays silent. The planted-defect test mutates the source with `sem_mutate` (`min` to `max`, wrong multiplier). Documented, not guarded: tied labels duplicate the diffLL, serial and parallel indirect effects are not testable, `tests$converged` is always `TRUE`. Reverting the three R files fails six test blocks. 3318 passed / 0 failed / 3 skipped; 10/10 CI.
ci_timeouts: 2026-10-09 — PR #103 squash-merged to dev `f2f6bbd`: `timeout-minutes` on lint (15), pkgdown (30), test-coverage (30), noSuggests (30) and the R-CMD-check matrix (45), set at 3-6x the slowest healthy run. Cause: #102's pkgdown sat 29 min in apt-get because azure.archive.ubuntu.com ran 25-100x slow (30.9 MB in 5 min 15 s vs 12 s), and no timeout meant the 360 min default. revdep-check and rhub left unchanged. The timeout firing was not exercised.
docs_row_identity: 2026-10-09 — PRs #98 (30 internal dot-* Rd pages hidden via @noRd), #99 (runnable cluster examples, refcard/cookbook pointers, roxygen link cleanup), #100 (extract_mediation(<lmerMod>) rejects fits that kept different individuals via rownames(model.frame()) comparison; default 1..n row names exempt; 8 edge-case tests) squash-merged to dev (`ee6666d`, `df15f54`, `9ce8bcc`). Known vague errors left by choice: J = 2 clusters, factor treatment. Unrun: urlchecker (github.com times out locally).
pkgdown_leak_audit: 2026-08-22 — cross-repo audit found the medfit PR #60 pkgdown leak pattern (pkgdown::package_mds() hardcodes README/LICENSE/NEWS/cran-comments as the only skipped root .md files, so CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/GEMINI.md and stray planning docs get published) was NOT unique to medfit — present in probmed, rmediation, medrobust, mediationverse too. Fixed source (pre-build `rm -f` of agent-instruction files + `.Rbuildignore`d moves of movable planning docs into `planning/`) via probmed #36, rmediation #32, mediationverse #22, medrobust #30 — all merged, worktrees/branches cleaned up. Second, larger issue found mid-fix: `clean: false` on every repo's `JamesIves/github-pages-deploy-action` step means an already-published leaked page never self-heals even after the source fix merges — it just stays orphaned on `gh-pages` forever. Purged 97 already-published leaked/orphaned files directly from live `gh-pages` branches across all 5 repos (medfit 2, probmed 3, rmediation 24, medrobust 52, mediationverse 16) via scratch clones + targeted `git rm` + direct push (not a PR — `gh-pages` is a generated deploy branch, not reviewed). medrobust's purge included ~20 stale `dev/` planning docs (PLAN-*/SPEC-*/ISSUE-* from a ~2026-06 build) unrelated to the CLAUDE.md pattern, found only by listing the full live tree rather than trusting the originally-scoped file list. `clean: false` itself was intentionally left as-is (not the audit's scope) — a future leak of a NEW file type will still require a manual purge; only the already-known patterns are closed out.
release_0.4.0: 2026-08-23 — v0.4.0 released (GitHub, not CRAN yet). PR #61 (dev→main, merge-commit `9ac7684`) — 17/17 checks green including a strict pre-release gate: `devtools::test()` 931+ pass/0 fail, `devtools::check(cran=TRUE, --run-donttest, DEPENDS_ONLY/SUGGESTS_ONLY/CRAN_INCOMING(_REMOTE))` = 0/0/0, `urlchecker::url_check()` clean (18/18), `spelling::spell_check_package()` clean. Tag `v0.4.0` pushed, GitHub release published (`--latest`, not a prerelease), release notes = NEWS.md 0.4.0 section (regmedint engine adapter, `engine_args`, first-class `m_star`, analytical regmedint SEs, `BootstrapResult` validator bug fix). dev fast-forwarded to match main (`9ac7684`), fully synced. No CRAN submission planned yet for 0.4.0 — GitHub-only release, same pattern as 0.3.1.
